From e2bbb8a19af8cf77b557bbfb2c220f5c89136d21 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: overdoingism <overdoingism@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 20:43:05 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] server, kv-cache: park the resident idle slots at the top of
 a unified KV cache (LLAMA_SERVER_PARK_IDLE_SLOTS)

#210 keeps an idle slot's context resident in a unified KV cache instead of saving and clearing it when a new task
starts.  A sequence that then runs alone no longer starts in an empty cache: its cells land after the resident ones, and
its attention range (n_kv) covers them too.  Flash attention's KV tiling and split depend on the cell indices and on n_kv,
so near-ties resolve differently.  Two one-at-a-time rounds of the same 16 requests agreed on 4/16 with resident idle
slots, and on 16/16 with LLAMA_SERVER_LAZY_IDLE_SLOTS=0 (gfx1201, Qwen3.8-27B + DFlash2, 4 slots).

The KV cache can now park a sequence.  llama_memory_seq_park() (staging API in llama-ext.h) moves its cells to the top of
the cache, below the sequences parked before it, with a device copy of the K/V rows and the cell state.  New cells are
only taken below the lowest parked cell, and get_n_kv() stops below it.  Parking and unparking keep the parked sequences
together at the top.  llama_memory_can_park() tells whether a cache supports it: one stream, cells it does not share,
V not transposed, no sliding window.

When a task starts, the server parks the idle slots and moves the slots that run back to the low cells.  A sequence that
runs alone then sits in the same cells and attends over the same range as when the idle slots are saved and cleared, so
it gives the same output, and the switch stays a device copy instead of a round trip through the host prompt cache.
- An idle slot that cannot be parked (its cells are not one run, or there is no room) is saved and cleared as before.
- A slot that cannot come back down frees room by clearing the least recently used idle slots.
- A KV cache that does not support parking keeps #210's lazy idle slots unchanged.
- The draft context is not parked: it does not decide the output, and a sliding-window draft cache reuses its cells.

LLAMA_SERVER_PARK_IDLE_SLOTS=0 keeps #210's behaviour; LLAMA_KV_PARK_DEBUG=1 logs every move and every refusal.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
